Follow @AGENTS.md, especially "Database, PR and Release Rules (Automatic)".
Apply it even when the feature prompt omits database or deployment requirements.

- Assess persisted EF entity/DbContext/mapping changes automatically. Use
  `.agents/skills/tct-ef-migration/SKILL.md` when schema may change.
- Include needed reviewed migrations, generated metadata and snapshot in the
  same feature PR; validate on disposable MariaDB and preserve existing data.
- The owner reviews/merges feature PRs unless separately authorized. CI success
  does not authorize merge, changing the deployment gate or bypassing the pipeline.
- Verify the actual release job, deployment gate, public commit marker and
  readiness before reporting production updated. A skipped release is not a deploy.

AGENTS.md owns the complete policy; this is the Cursor always-applied adapter.
